FREE                                                     [2.40, 3.0]
----

Format:      FREE [d:]

Purpose:      Displays the  total disk  space, total disk space used
        and total disk space free of the specified or default drive.

Use:          If  a drive  is given,  then the  volume name  of that
        drive is  displayed, along  with the  total disk  space, the
        used disk space and the free disk space.

             If  no drive is given, then the default drive is assum-
        ed.

             When the drive is mapped to a disk  image file,  to the
        RAM disk,  or is a ghost drive of another one,  a note about
        it is printed after the volume line.

             When the drive is in zero allocation  information  mode
        (see HELP RALLOC),  no space information is available and  a
        note is printed instead of the figures.


Examples:

        FREE A:

             Volume in drive A: has no name
                 10216K total disk space
                  5100K used for files
                  5116K available disk space

        Displays the total, used and free disk space on drive A:.
